nts\",\"item\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Over the Rainbow Runs\"}]}]}},\"acf\":{\"additional_heading\":\"\",\"location_name\":\"Jacob Hamblin Park\",\"address\":\"566 N 100 E, Kanab, UT 84741\",\"contact_number\":\"\",\"start_datetime\":\"October 14, 2023 9:00 am\",\"multi_day_event\":false,\"recurrance\":\"\",\"category\":{\"term_id\":12,\"name\":\"Sports &amp; Recreation\",\"slug\":\"sports-recreation\",\"term_group\":0,\"term_taxonomy_id\":12,\"taxonomy\":\"event_categories\",\"description\":\"#FE00F4\",\"parent\":0,\"count\":0,\"filter\":\"raw\"},\"redirect_url\":\"\",\"document_download\":false,\"information_block\":\"<div>The Over the Rainbow Runs are a pair of trail races, 10K and Half Marathon in length,\\u00a0set among the wildly beautiful bluffs above Kanab, Utah. We are entirely volunteer-operated, with all proceeds benefiting the Kane County Children&#8217;s Justice Center.\\u00a0 Our event fosters community and inclusivity while enjoying our beautiful public lands!<\\/div>\\n<div><\\/div>\\n<div>For more information and to register:\\u00a0<a href=\\\"http:\\/\\/overtherainbowruns.wordpress.com\\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\" data-saferedirecturl=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.google.com\\/url?q=http:\\/\\/overtherainbowruns.wordpress.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1680134105238000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2GtkfYn1VTx7Kbkc00pcUT\\\">overtherainbowruns.<wbr \\/>wordpress.com<\\/a><\\/div>\\n<div><\\/div>\\n<div><\\/div>\\n<div><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" class=\\\"alignnone wp-image-13145 size-full\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer.png\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" width=\\\"1294\\\" height=\\\"2000\\\" srcset=\\\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer.png 1294w, \\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer-194x300.png 194w, \\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer-663x1024.png 663w, \\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer-768x1187.png 768w, \\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/2023-Full-Flyer-994x1536.png 994w\\\" sizes=\\\"(max-width: 1294px) 100vw, 1294px\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\n\",\"information_heading\":\"\",\"information_block_1\":\"\",\"gallery\":false,\"information_block_2\":\"\",\"related_events\":\"\"},\"featured_image_url\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/09\\/Screenshot-2021-09-07-092327-768x531.jpg\",\"_links\":{\"self\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/events\\/7985\"}],\"collection\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/events\"}],\"about\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/types\\/events\"}],\"author\":[{\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/users\\/8\"}],\"wp:featuredmedia\":[{\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/media\\/7988\"}],\"wp:attachment\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/media?parent=7985\"}],\"wp:term\":[{\"taxonomy\":\"event_categories\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/event_categories?post=7985\"}],\"curies\":[{\"name\":\"wp\",\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/api.w.org\\/{rel}\",\"templated\":true}]}}',1,'2023-10-05 04:52:01','2023-10-06 22:56:14'),(56,'North Rim &#8211; Grand Canyon Day Use','vsu','3664',162,'The North Rim of Grand Canyon National Park transitions to day-use operations beginning Oct. 16. This change occurs yearly as the North Rim prepares for its seasonal closure that lasts from Oct. 15 to May 15. Visitors should be aware that day-use operations means there will be no overnight lodging and limited services.\nThe South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions. Access to the South Rim is from Arizona Highway 64 while access to the North Rim is from Arizona Highway 67, this is on the ‘Utah’ side of the park. Entrance to the park is $30 per private vehicle and $12 for individuals entering by foot, motorcycle, or bicycle. The permit is good for 7 days and is valid at both the North and South Rims. For $50 you can purchase a Grand Canyon National Park Annual Pass. Or for $80 you can purchase a National Parks and Federal Recreational Lands Pass that is good for national parks across the United States.\nNorth Rim roads are closed to all vehicles between December 1st and May 15th, and no visitor services are available. During these winter months backpackers, snowshoers, and cross-country skiers are permitted to use the North Rim Campground, provided a backcountry use permit has been obtained in advance. – These permits are available through the South Rim Backcountry Information Center. (e-mail us or call 928-638-7875). The weather at the park can be extreme during the winter and summer months. During the winter, snow is common in the higher elevations, especially the North Rim. Temperatures drop well below freezing at times. The Inner Gorge of the Grand Canyon rarely sees snow and has milder temperatures during the winter. The summer months are extremely hot, especially in the Inner Gorge. Temperatures here can reach past 100 degrees Fahrenheit. There are two rainy seasons at the canyon, one during the winter and one during the late summer. The summer storms are monsoon-like and often develop into thunderstorms. Flash flooding can occur on the canyon floor so hikers should be very careful when hiking in inclement weather. Grand Canyon weather forecasts can be checked at visitor centers and ranger stations before hiking into the canyon.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2023-10-15 00:00:00',NULL,'{\"id\":3664,\"date\":\"2020-02-25T22:37:55\",\"date_gmt\":\"2020-02-25T22:37:55\",\"guid\":{\"rendered\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/?post_type=events&#038;p=3664\"},\"modified\":\"2023-04-03T14:06:43\",\"modified_gmt\":\"2023-04-03T20:06:43\",\"slug\":\"north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\",\"status\":\"publish\",\"type\":\"events\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\",\"title\":{\"rendered\":\"North Rim &#8211; Grand Canyon Day Use\"},\"content\":{\"rendered\":\"\",\"protected\":false},\"excerpt\":{\"rendered\":\"\",\"protected\":false},\"author\":8,\"featured_media\":8818,\"template\":\"\",\"event_categories\":[],\"yoast_head\":\"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v18.6 - https:\\/\\/yoast.com\\/wordpress\\/plugins\\/seo\\/ -->\\n<title>North Rim - Grand Canyon Day Use | Visit Southern Utah<\\/title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"robots\\\" content=\\\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\\\" \\/>\\n<link rel=\\\"canonical\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:locale\\\" content=\\\"en_US\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:type\\\" content=\\\"article\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:title\\\" content=\\\"North Rim - Grand Canyon Day Use | Visit Southern Utah\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:description\\\" content=\\\"The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:url\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:site_name\\\" content=\\\"Visit Southern Utah\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"article:modified_time\\\" content=\\\"2023-04-03T20:06:43+00:00\\\" \\/>\\n<meta property=\\\"og:image\\\" content=\\\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2020\\/02\\/20211015_140211_05_saved.jpg\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta property=\\\"og:image:width\\\" content=\\\"2149\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta property=\\\"og:image:height\\\" content=\\\"2149\\\" \\/>\\n\\t<meta property=\\\"og:image:type\\\" content=\\\"image\\/jpeg\\\" \\/>\\n<meta name=\\\"twitter:card\\\" content=\\\"summary_large_image\\\" \\/>\\n<!-- \\/ Yoast SEO plugin. -->\",\"yoast_head_json\":{\"title\":\"North Rim - Grand Canyon Day Use | Visit Southern Utah\",\"description\":\"The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions\",\"robots\":{\"index\":\"index\",\"follow\":\"follow\",\"max-snippet\":\"max-snippet:-1\",\"max-image-preview\":\"max-image-preview:large\",\"max-video-preview\":\"max-video-preview:-1\"},\"canonical\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\",\"og_locale\":\"en_US\",\"og_type\":\"article\",\"og_title\":\"North Rim - Grand Canyon Day Use | Visit Southern Utah\",\"og_description\":\"The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions\",\"og_url\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\",\"og_site_name\":\"Visit Southern Utah\",\"article_modified_time\":\"2023-04-03T20:06:43+00:00\",\"og_image\":[{\"width\":2149,\"height\":2149,\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2020\\/02\\/20211015_140211_05_saved.jpg\",\"type\":\"image\\/jpeg\"}],\"twitter_card\":\"summary_large_image\",\"schema\":{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/#website\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/\",\"name\":\"Visit Southern Utah\",\"description\":\"Kanab - Magically Unspoiled\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/search\\/{search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":\"required name=search_term_string\"}],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/#primaryimage\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"url\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2020\\/02\\/20211015_140211_05_saved.jpg\",\"contentUrl\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2020\\/02\\/20211015_140211_05_saved.jpg\",\"width\":2149,\"height\":2149},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/#webpage\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\",\"name\":\"North Rim - Grand Canyon Day Use | Visit Southern Utah\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/#primaryimage\"},\"datePublished\":\"2020-02-25T22:37:55+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2023-04-03T20:06:43+00:00\",\"description\":\"The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/#breadcrumb\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"ReadAction\",\"target\":[\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/north-rim-grand-canyon-opening-day\\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Events\",\"item\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/events\\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"North Rim &#8211; Grand Canyon Day Use\"}]}]}},\"acf\":{\"additional_heading\":\"\",\"location_name\":\"North Rim-Grand Canyon National Park\",\"address\":\"\",\"contact_number\":\"\",\"start_datetime\":\"October 15, 2023 12:00 am\",\"multi_day_event\":false,\"recurrance\":\"\",\"category\":{\"term_id\":11,\"name\":\"Parks &amp; Outdoor\",\"slug\":\"parks-outdoor\",\"term_group\":0,\"term_taxonomy_id\":11,\"taxonomy\":\"event_categories\",\"description\":\"#00FE3B\",\"parent\":0,\"count\":0,\"filter\":\"raw\"},\"redirect_url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/north-rim.htm\",\"document_download\":false,\"information_block\":\"<p class=\\\"gnt_ar_b_p\\\">The North Rim of Grand Canyon National Park transitions to day-use operations beginning Oct. 16. This change occurs yearly as the North Rim prepares for its seasonal closure that lasts from Oct. 15 to May 15.\\u00a0Visitors should be aware that day-use operations means there will be no overnight lodging and <strong>limited services<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<p>The South Rim of the Grand Canyon is open all year while the North Rim is open mid-May through mid-October due to harsh winter weather conditions. Access to the South Rim is from Arizona Highway 64 while access to the North Rim is from Arizona Highway 67, this is on the \\u2018Utah\\u2019 side of the park. Entrance to the park is $30\\u00a0per private vehicle and $12 for individuals entering by foot, motorcycle, or bicycle. The permit is good for 7 days and is valid at both the North and South Rims. For $50\\u00a0you can purchase a Grand Canyon National Park Annual Pass. Or for $80 you can purchase a National Parks and Federal Recreational Lands Pass that is good for national parks across the United States.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>North Rim roads are closed to all vehicles between December 1st and May 15th, and no visitor services are available.<\\/strong>\\u00a0During these winter months backpackers, snowshoers, and cross-country skiers are permitted to use the North Rim Campground, provided a\\u00a0<a id=\\\"CP___PAGEID=1902011,backcountry-permit.htm,11006|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/backcountry-permit.htm\\\">backcountry use permit<\\/a>\\u00a0has been obtained in advance. \\u2013 These permits are available through the South Rim Backcountry Information Center. (<a id=\\\"\\/common\\/utilities\\/sendmail\\/sendemail.cfm?o=4C97D8BAA2D1A6BFB4B503BCB710A4BB&amp;r=\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/north-rim.htm|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/common\\/utilities\\/sendmail\\/sendemail.cfm?o=4C97D8BAA2D1A6BFB4B503BCB710A4BB&amp;r=\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/north-rim.htm\\\">e-mail us<\\/a> or call 928-638-7875). The weather at the park can be extreme during the winter and summer months. During the winter, snow is common in the higher elevations, especially the North Rim. Temperatures drop well below freezing at times. The Inner Gorge of the Grand Canyon rarely sees snow and has milder temperatures during the winter. The summer months are extremely hot, especially in the Inner Gorge. Temperatures here can reach past 100 degrees Fahrenheit. There are two rainy seasons at the canyon, one during the winter and one during the late summer. The summer storms are monsoon-like and often develop into thunderstorms. Flash flooding can occur on the canyon floor so hikers should be very careful when hiking in inclement weather. Grand Canyon weather forecasts can be checked at visitor centers and ranger stations before hiking into the canyon.<\\/p>\\n\",\"information_heading\":\"\",\"information_block_1\":\"\",\"gallery\":[{\"ID\":2905,\"id\":2905,\"title\":\"Grand-Canyon-toroweap-KCOT-KCOT\",\"filename\":\"Grand-Canyon-toroweap-KCOT-KCOT.jpg\",\"filesize\":459080,\"url\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2019\\/08\\/Grand-Canyon-toroweap-KCOT-KCOT.jpg\",\"link\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/attractions\\/grand-canyon-national-park\\/grand-canyon-toroweap-kcot-kcot\\/\",\"alt\":\"\",\"a