ow hoodoos happen!\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"32962\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Bryce Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"31A09312-CF1F-49CF-584B28EDFDDC6A15\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:50','2025-03-21 18:08:50'),(77,'Plaza Ranger Talk','nps','45A44BDD-01C1-850A-432168C063FD977B',2,'Come join a Ranger at the Visitor Center Plaza for a talk on a random topic of the ranger\'s choosing, covering natural, cultural, or historical resources. \nThis program will be cancelled by thunderstorms or extreme cold weather. \nWheelchair Accessible.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisitor Center Plaza',37.6404,-112.17,'brca_information@nps.gov',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-03-02 00:00:00','2025-03-02 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"109845\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-02\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-02\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-02\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-05-03\",\"latitude\":\"37.640387\",\"longitude\":\"-112.169642\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"Plaza Ranger Talk\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"brca_information@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p>Come join a Ranger at the Visitor Center Plaza for a talk on a random topic of the ranger\'s choosing, covering natural, cultural, or historical resources.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>This program will be cancelled by thunderstorms or extreme cold weather.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Wheelchair Accessible.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Visitor Center Plaza\",\"tags\":[],\"types\":[\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250302T070000Z;UNTIL=20250503T060000Z;FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;BYDAY=SU,MO,WE,TH,FR,SA;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"brca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-01T17:11:10.733\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-01T17:16:53.18\",\"createuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"02:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"03:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-21\",\"2025-03-22\",\"2025-03-23\",\"2025-03-24\",\"2025-03-26\",\"2025-03-27\",\"2025-03-28\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-03-30\",\"2025-03-31\",\"2025-04-02\",\"2025-04-03\",\"2025-04-04\",\"2025-04-05\",\"2025-04-06\",\"2025-04-07\",\"2025-04-09\",\"2025-04-10\",\"2025-04-11\",\"2025-04-12\",\"2025-04-13\",\"2025-04-14\",\"2025-04-16\",\"2025-04-17\",\"2025-04-18\",\"2025-04-19\",\"2025-04-20\",\"2025-04-21\",\"2025-04-23\",\"2025-04-24\",\"2025-04-25\",\"2025-04-26\",\"2025-04-27\",\"2025-04-28\",\"2025-04-30\",\"2025-05-01\",\"2025-05-02\",\"2025-05-03\"],\"images\":[],\"imageidlist\":\"\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Bryce Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"45A44BDD-01C1-850A-432168C063FD977B\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:50','2025-03-21 18:08:50'),(78,'Full Moon Hike','nps','AD2AB901-BDE2-9D72-1A2341056A152EEB',2,'Typically offered year-round at sunset as weather permits. Those planning to join a ranger-led full moon hike at Bryce Canyon National Park can make reservations online via Recreation.gov. Tickets for each month’s hike are released in two phases, 14 and 5 days in advance.This is a \"ranger\'s choice\" hike and can range from an easy hike along the rim of the plateau to a more strenuous hike that descends down into the canyon along steep and rocky trails. More information will be given on the day of the event. Hikes are typically 1 to 2 miles.For more information on full moon hikes, including schedules and how to participate, please visit our Full Moon Hikes page.\nDue to the nature of this special activity all participants must agree to the following rules:\n\nChildren 7 and younger are not permitted.\nHiking boots or hiking shoes (lug soles) in good condition are required for your safety and the safety of Park Staff and other Participant(s).\nWhite light flashlights, headlamps are not allowed to be used during the hike (you may bring them for later use). Red light flashlights and headlamps are permitted as necessary. Flash photography may be permitted under key restrictions.\nBring drinking water and a jacket - night time temperatures can be cold.\nDue to steep and rocky trails this activity is not wheelchair accessible.\n\nWindchill may cancel this event.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeeting location and route varies.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-04-12 00:00:00','2025-04-12 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"104205\",\"date\":\"2025-04-12\",\"datestart\":\"2025-04-12\",\"dateend\":\"2025-04-12\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-04-12\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2023-09-29\",\"latitude\":\"\",\"longitude\":\"\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"true\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"Go to Recreation.gov\",\"infourl\":\"\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"Starting time depends on moonrise and Ranger\'s preference.\",\"title\":\"Full Moon Hike\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p>Typically offered year-round at sunset as weather permits.\\u00a0Those planning to join a ranger-led full moon hike at Bryce Canyon National Park can make reservations online via <a id=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info\\\" data-cke-saved-href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info\\\">Recreation.gov<\\/a>. Tickets for each month\\u2019s hike are released in two phases, 14 and 5 days in advance.<br \\/><br \\/>This is a \\\"ranger\'s choice\\\" hike and can range from an easy hike along the rim of the plateau to a more strenuous hike that descends down into the canyon along steep and rocky trails. More information will be given on the day of the event. Hikes are typically 1 to 2 miles.<br \\/><br \\/><strong>For more information on full moon hikes, including schedules and how to participate, please visit our <a id=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm\\\" data-cke-saved-href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm\\\">Full Moon Hikes<\\/a> page.<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<h4>Due to the nature of this special activity all participants must agree to the following rules:<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Children 7 and younger are not permitted.<\\/li>\\n<li>Hiking boots or hiking shoes (lug soles) in good condition are required for your safety and the safety of Park Staff and other Participant(s).<\\/li>\\n<li>White light flashlights, headlamps\\u00a0are not\\u00a0allowed to be used during the hike (you may bring them for later use). Red light flashlights and headlamps are permitted as necessary. Flash photography may be permitted under key restrictions.<\\/li>\\n<li>Bring drinking water and a jacket - night time temperatures can be cold.<\\/li>\\n<li>Due to steep and rocky trails this activity is not wheelchair accessible.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Windchill may cancel this event.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Meeting location and route varies.\",\"tags\":[],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Guided Tour\",\"Hike\",\"Talk\",\"Walk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"brca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-09-30T15:59:31.18\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-01-04T11:44:37.043\",\"createuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"07:30 PM\",\"timeend\":\"08:30 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-04-12\"],\"images\":[{\"ima