res can be cold.\nDue to steep and rocky trails this activity is not wheelchair accessible.\n\n Windchill will cancel this event.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeeting location and route varies.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-12-04 00:00:00','2025-12-04 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"104213\",\"date\":\"2025-12-04\",\"datestart\":\"2025-12-04\",\"dateend\":\"2025-12-04\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-12-04\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2023-09-29\",\"latitude\":\"\",\"longitude\":\"\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"true\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"Go to Recreation.gov\",\"infourl\":\"\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"Starting time depends on moonrise and Ranger\'s preference.\",\"title\":\"Full Moon Hike\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p>Typically offered year-round at sunset as weather permits.\\u00a0Those planning to join a ranger-led full moon hike at Bryce Canyon National Park can make reservations online via <a id=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info\\\" data-cke-saved-href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.recreation.gov\\/ticket\\/facility\\/10112209?tab=info\\\">Recreation.gov<\\/a>. Tickets for each month\\u2019s hike are released in two phases, 14 and 5 days in advance.<br \\/><br \\/>This is a \\\"ranger\'s choice\\\" hike and can range from an easy hike along the rim of the plateau to a more strenuous hike that descends down into the canyon along steep and rocky trails. More information will be given on the day of the event. Hikes are typically 1 to 2 miles.<br \\/><br \\/><strong>For more information on full moon hikes, including schedules and how to participate, please visit our <a id=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm|\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm\\\" data-cke-saved-href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/brca\\/planyourvisit\\/fullmoonhikes.htm\\\">Full Moon Hikes<\\/a> page.<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<h4>Due to the nature of this special activity all participants must agree to the following rules:<\\/h4>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Children 7 and younger are not permitted.<\\/li>\\n<li>Hiking boots or hiking shoes (lug soles) in good condition are required for your safety and the safety of Park Staff and other Participant(s).<\\/li>\\n<li>White light flashlights, headlamps\\u00a0are not\\u00a0allowed to be used during the hike (you may bring them for later use). Red light flashlights and headlamps are permitted as necessary. Flash photography may be permitted under key restrictions.<\\/li>\\n<li>Bring drinking water and a jacket - night time temperatures can be cold.<\\/li>\\n<li>Due to steep and rocky trails this activity is not wheelchair accessible.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>\\u00a0Windchill will cancel this event.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Meeting location and route varies.\",\"tags\":[],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Guided Tour\",\"Hike\",\"Talk\",\"Walk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"brca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-09-30T16:13:31.447\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-01-04T11:54:51.673\",\"createuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"eblair@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"05:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"06:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-12-04\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"38516\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/410F7A13-90CD-DC4A-63B644303AE9B064.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/410F7A13-90CD-DC4A-63B644303AE9B064.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Moonrse over Bryce Canyon amplitheaters\",\"caption\":\"Moonrse over Bryce Canyon amplitheaters\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"38516\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Bryce Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"ADAAEFAE-0250-6B93-3853F19880B0F607\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:51','2025-03-21 18:08:51'),(88,'Guided Snowshoe Tour','nps','C2A73B63-BA32-A479-A9E61136DFFBD012',3,'Join us for a beginner-friendly Guided Snowshoe Tour and connect with the natural beauty found within the park. Participants will hike a distance of 1-mile roundtrip through snowy terrain, learning from rangers as they stop along the way to share information about the Monument. Approximately halfway through the hike, the group will stop for a 15-minute Ranger program. In total, the entire experience will last about one hour and thirty minutes.\nThe equipment, including snowshoes and a pair of ski poles, are available to all participants at no cost. There is no fee for joining a Guided Snowshoe Tour, however, there is an entrance fee to visit the park. All groups will be required to pay an entrance fee of $25 per vehicle. Alternatively, Interagency Annual Passes, also called America the Beautiful Pass, will waive the per-person fee of visitors traveling together in a single vehicle.\\r\\n\\r\\nNorth View Overlook (LAT/LONG: 37.656556, -112.834466)',37.6566,-112.834,NULL,NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/cebr/planyourvisit/winter-snowshoe-2025.htm',NULL,NULL,'2024-12-27 00:00:00','2025-03-22 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Special Event\",\"eventid\":\"106578\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2024-12-27\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-22\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2024-12-27\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-22\",\"latitude\":\"37.656556\",\"longitude\":\"-112.834466\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"true\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/guided-snowshoe-tours-at-cedar-breaks-national-monument-tickets-1095688496789?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"regresinfo\":\"Visit our event page on EventBrite to register for the free snowshoe tour. You will receive a confirmation email with more details after registration.\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/cebr\\/planyourvisit\\/winter-snowshoe-2025.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"Tours are free of charge; however, as a federal fee area, all groups require an entrance pass to Cedar Breaks. Entrance passes are $25 per vehicle. Interagency Annual or America the Beautiful passes waive the entry fee of all individuals traveling together in one vehicle.\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"Guided Snowshoe Tour\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p>Join us for a beginner-friendly Guided Snowshoe Tour and connect with the natural beauty found within the park. Participants will hike a distance of 1-mile roundtrip through snowy terrain, learning from rangers as they stop along the way to share information about the Monument. Approximately halfway through the hike, the group will stop for a 15-minute Ranger program. In total, the entire experience will last about one hour and thirty minutes.<\\/p>\\n<p>The equipment, including snowshoes and a pair of ski poles, are available to all participants at no cost. There is no fee for joining a Guided Snowshoe Tour, however, there is an entrance fee to visit the park.\\u00a0All groups will be required to pay an entrance fee of $25 per vehicle. Alternatively, Interagency Annual Passes, also called America the Beautiful Pass, will waive the per-person fee of visitors traveling together in a single vehicle.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"North View Overlook (LAT\\/LONG: 37.656556, -112.834466)\",\"tags\":[],\"types\":[\"Guided Tour\",\"Hike\",\"Talk\",\"Walk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20241227T070000Z;UNTIL=20250322T060000Z;FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;BYDAY=FR,SA;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"cebr\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-12-04T15:57:56.473\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2024-12-04T16:08:48.973\",\"createuser\":\"agutierrez@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"agutierrez@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"c716da99-223b-4b01-bd6c-0300d325b18e\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"10:00 AM\",\"timeend\":\"11:30 AM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"},{\"timestart\":\"12:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"01:30 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"},{\"timestart\":\"02:30 PM\",\"timeend\":\"04:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-21\",\"2025-03-22\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"45444\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/C2FE483D-9CD6-8DD8-2744DBAB5F52B432.png\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/C2FE483D-9CD6-8DD8-2744DBAB5F52B432.png\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"A pair of snowshoes and ski poles stands in the snow against the amphitheater landscape.\",\"caption\":\"Snowshoes rest in the snow in front of the scenic amphitheater.\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\\/Gutierrez\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"45444\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Cedar Breaks National Monument\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"C2A73B63-BA32-A479-A9E61136DFFBD012\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:52','2025-03-21 18:08:52'),(89,'Night Sky Tours','nps','C401709C-065E-4BA7-2DF2605971858B97',3,'Come be an astronomer! Join the Rangers of Cedar Breaks under a sky of stars, planets, and nebulas. Experience a night of wonder and observe astronomical features through a telescope.\\r\\n\\r\\nNorth View Overlook (LAT/LONG: 37.656556, -112.834466)',37.6566,-112.834,NULL,NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/cebr/planyourvisit/dark-sky-tours-2025.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-15 00:00:00','2025-04-27 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Special Event\",\"eventid\":\"106583\",\"date\":\"2025-03-22\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-15\",\"dateend\":\"2025-04-27\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-15\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-04-27\",\"latitude\":\"37.656556\",\"longitude\":\"-112.834466\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"true\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/night-sky-tours-tickets-1105728827689?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"regresinfo\":\"Visit our event page on EventBrite to register for the free snowshoe tour. You will receive a confirmation email with more details after registration.\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/cebr\\/planyourvisit\\/dark-sky-tours-2025.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"Tours are free of charge; however, as a federal fee area, all groups require an entrance pass to Cedar Breaks. Entrance passes are $25 per vehicle. Interagency Annual or America the Beautiful passes waive the entry fee of all individuals traveling together in one vehicle.\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"Night Sky Tours\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p>Come be an astronomer! Join the Rangers of Cedar Breaks under a sky of stars, planets, and nebulas. Experience a night of wonder and observe astronomical features through a telescope.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"North View Overlook (LAT\\/LONG: 37.656556, -112.834466)\",\"tags\":[],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Guided Tour\",\"Management\\/Planning\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250315T060000Z;UNTIL=20250427T060000Z;FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;BYDAY=SA;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"cebr\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-12-04T16:35:45.383\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-05T13:27:36.557\",\"createuser\":\"agutierrez@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"agutierrez@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"c716da99-223b-4b01-bd6c-0300d325b18e\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"08:30 PM\",\"timeend\":\"10:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-22\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-04-05\",\"2025-04-12\",\"2025-04-19\",\"2025-04-26\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"45447\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/C3FD3C6F-B429-86B3-C54E3E5D255C5C37.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/