 Hwy 89. Cross the bridge and travel a quarter of a mile. The turnoff will be on your left, indicated by a brown \\\"hiking: symbol sign. Park along the road near the trailhead.\",\"tags\":[\"Glen Canyon National Recreation Area\",\"hanging garden\",\"trailhead\",\"The Chains\",\"Guided Hike\",\"sunset hike\",\"glca2025\"],\"types\":[\"Guided Tour\",\"Hike\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"glca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-02-26T13:15:04.643\",\"datetimeupdated\":null,\"createuser\":\"escroggs@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"05:30 PM\",\"timeend\":\"06:30 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-22\"],\"images\":[],\"imageidlist\":\"\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Glen Canyon National Recreation Area\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"A2B2333D-C2F4-05B7-7B66D20FD9A26484\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:53','2025-03-21 18:08:53'),(94,'Hanging Garden Ranger Guided Hike','nps','A2BDD98A-D970-BC9B-0D589A2F7404F7BA',4,'Join a park ranger for a moderate hike through a desert landscape to learn more about the plants, animals, geology, and history of Glen Canyon.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeet at the trailhead for the Hanging Garden trail. From Caarl Hayden Visitor Center, turn left on to Hwy 89. Cross the bridge and travel a quarter of a mile. The turnoff will be on your left, indicated by a brown \"hiking: symbol sign. Park along the road near the trailhead.',36.9367,-111.476,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-03-27 00:00:00','2025-03-27 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"109677\",\"date\":\"2025-03-27\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-04-05\",\"latitude\":\"36.936712\",\"longitude\":\"-111.476172\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"All times are Mountain Standard Time. Make sure your clock is set to AZ time.\",\"title\":\"Hanging Garden Ranger Guided Hike\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"x_elementToProof\\\" data-ogsc=\\\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\\\" data-olk-copy-source=\\\"MessageBody\\\">Join a park ranger for a moderate hike through a desert landscape to learn more about the plants, animals, geology, and history of Glen Canyon.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Meet at the trailhead for the Hanging Garden trail. From Caarl Hayden Visitor Center, turn left on to Hwy 89. Cross the bridge and travel a quarter of a mile. The turnoff will be on your left, indicated by a brown \\\"hiking: symbol sign. Park along the road near the trailhead.\",\"tags\":[\"Glen Canyon National Recreation Area\",\"hanging garden\",\"trailhead\",\"The Chains\",\"Guided Hike\",\"sunset hike\",\"glca2025\"],\"types\":[\"Guided Tour\",\"Hike\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250327T070000Z;UNTIL=20250405T070000Z;FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;BYDAY=TH,FR,SA;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"glca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-02-26T13:16:20.993\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-19T09:21:51.177\",\"createuser\":\"escroggs@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"escroggs@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"05:30 PM\",\"timeend\":\"06:30 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-27\",\"2025-03-28\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-04-03\",\"2025-04-04\",\"2025-04-05\"],\"images\":[],\"imageidlist\":\"\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Glen Canyon National Recreation Area\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"A2BDD98A-D970-BC9B-0D589A2F7404F7BA\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:53','2025-03-21 18:08:53'),(95,'South Rim Village | Canyon Connections Ranger Talk — Grand Canyon Visitor Center - free','nps','B478CB1F-F61E-2BB9-BDC801F6A1486DD1',5,'Canyon Connections -Ranger\'s Talk (Topic Varies) — Meet at Grand Canyon Visitor Center \nDiscover a deeper connection to the Grand Canyon. Join a ranger to dive into the canyon\'s diverse ecosystems, rich cultural heritage, or ever-changing landscape. Topics change daily. Come curious, leave inspired! Program may include a short walk to Mather Point or along the Canyon Rim Trail.\nProgram duration: 30 minutes. Presented daily. \nAccessible. Family friendly. Perfect program for Junior Rangers!\nThe program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult. This program is subject to cancellation due to inclement weather or when lightning danger is present. \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.',36.0591,-112.109,'grca_information@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/sr-programs.htm',NULL,NULL,'2024-10-28 00:00:00','2025-05-03 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"104840\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2024-10-28\",\"dateend\":\"2025-05-03\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2024-10-28\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-05-03\",\"latitude\":\"36.059129\",\"longitude\":\"-112.109296\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/sr-programs.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Canyon Connections Ranger Talk \\u2014 Grand Canyon Visitor Center - free\",\"contactname\":\"Park Information\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_information@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Canyon Connections -Ranger\'s Talk (Topic Varies) \\u2014 Meet at Grand Canyon Visitor Center<\\/strong>\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Discover a deeper connection to the Grand Canyon. Join a ranger to dive into the canyon\'s diverse ecosystems, rich cultural heritage, or ever-changing landscape. Topics change daily. Come curious, leave inspired! Program may include a short walk to Mather Point or along the Canyon Rim Trail.<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Program duration: 30 minutes. Presented daily.<\\/strong>\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Accessible. Family friendly. Perfect program for Junior Rangers!<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p>The program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult. This program is subject to cancellation due to inclement weather or when lightning danger is present.\\u00a0<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"From the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.\",\"tags\":[\"ranger activity\",\"Ranger Talk\",\"ranger program\",\"Grand Canyon\",\"Outdoor activities\",\"visitor center\",\"Visitor Activities\",\"visitor\",\"Junior Ranger\",\"Village\"],\"types\":[\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20241028T070000Z;UNTIL=20250503T070000Z;FREQ=DAILY;WKST=SU;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-10-20T16:36:49.733\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-01-18T11:56:41.983\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"d0ec81bc-529b-43b9-997a-9da8593be7f6\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"03:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"03:30 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-21\",\"2025-03-22\",\"2025-03-23\",\"2025-03-24\",\"2025-03-25\",\"2025-03-26\",\"2025-03-27\",\"2025-03-28\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-03-30\",\"2025-03-31\",\"2025-04-01\",\"2025-04-02\",\"2025-04-03\",\"2025-04-04\",\"2025-04-05\",\"2025-04-06\",\"2025-04-07\",\"2025-04-08\",\"2025-04-09\",\"2025-04-10\",\"2025-04-11\",\"2025-04-12\",\"2025-04-13\",\"2025-04-14\",\"2025-04-15\",\"2025-04-16\",\"2025-04-17\",\"2025-04-18\",\"2025-04-19\",\"2025-04-20\",\"2025-04-21\",\"2025-04-22\",\"2025-04-23\",\"2025-04-24\",\"2025-04-25\",\"2025-04-26\",\"2025-04-27\",\"2025-04-28\",\"2025-04-29\",\"2025-04-30\",\"2025-05-01\",\"2025-05-02\",\"2025-05-03\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"36932\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/5DA671A8-CCA5-574D-9E4844FA453BBB23.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/5DA671A8-CCA5-574D-9E4844FA453BBB23.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Map shows location of 4 public parking lots in relation to and surrounding the Visitor Center Plaza.\",\"caption\":\"Meet by the flagpole in front of the Visitor Center Building (in the center of the map).\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"36933\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/5DD286A1-D7DD-BEFE-A8BEB22BDD735907.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/5DD286A1-D7DD-BEFE-A8BEB22BDD735907.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"view down and across a snowy plaza with a long narrow building with a gabled roof on the right\",\"caption\":\"Grand Canyon Visitor Center on the South Rim of the park - during winter.\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\\/M. Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"},{\"imageid\":\"37165\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/193E7F65-C462-7928-E455896F9FE6CD6F.png\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/193E7F65-C462-7928-E455896F9FE6CD6F.png\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Park ranger is giving a program outdoors and conversing with visitors who are wearing winter clothes\",\"caption\":\"The 3 pm ranger program may be held indoors or outside, depending upon weather conditions.\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\\/M. Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"3\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"36932,36933,37165\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"B478CB1F-F61E-2BB9-BDC801F6A1486DD1\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(96,'South Rim Village | Geology Talk Ranger Program — Yavapai Geology Museum - free','nps','B42EEF91-F916-DB52-AC44BFB98B748002',5,'Grand Canyon Geology Talk Ranger ProgramEnhance your afternoon with quick insights into the geologic story of Grand Canyon at our \"Geo Glimpse\" ranger program - presented daily at 11 am. Meet in front of Yavapai Geology Museum. Learn how this immense canyon formed and the science behind the landscape. The program is 30 minutes long and is accessible. \n\nGrand Canyon is one-mile deep, up to 18 miles wide, 277 river miles long, and displays more than 20 layers of rock The layers tell stories of oceans, deserts, mountains, and swamps that were once here, brought into existence, then swept away over the vast expanse of time. \n\n\nGrand Canyon is a geologically young landscape being sculpted from very old rocks. Knowing some of the stories encoded in the rock layers enriches your understanding of our planet and enhances your experience at Grand Canyon.\n\nThe program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.  The Geology Talk is subject to cancellation due to inclement weather or when lightning danger is present.\n\n \\r\\n\\r\\nYavapai Point is located on Village Loop Road, in between Market Plaza and the Grand Canyon Visitor Center. From the far end of the Yavapai Point parking lot, by the shuttle bus stop, walk the paved path up the hill on your left to the stone museum building, perched on the edge of the canyon rim. Meet the ranger at 9 am, just outside of the building.',36.0661,-112.118,'grca_information@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/places/000/yavapai-geology-museum.htm',NULL,NULL,'2024-10-28 00:00:00','2025-05-03 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"104839\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2024-10-28\",\"dateend\":\"2025-05-03\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2024-10-28\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-05-03\",\"latitude\":\"36.066083\",\"longitude\":\"-112.117550\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/places\\/000\\/yavapai-geology-museum.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Geology Talk Ranger Program \\u2014 Yavapai Geology Museum - free\",\"contactname\":\"Ranger Program Coordinator\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_information@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<div class=\\\"Component text-content-size text-content-style ArticleTextGroup clearfix\\\">\\n<p>Grand Canyon Geology\\u00a0Talk Ranger Program<br \\/><br \\/>Enhance your afternoon with\\u00a0quick insights into the geologic story of Grand Canyon at our \\\"Geo Glimpse\\\" ranger program - presented daily at 11 am. Meet in front of Yavapai Geology Museum.\\u00a0Learn how this immense canyon formed and the science behind the landscape. The program is 30 minutes long and is accessible.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Grand Canyon\\u00a0is one-mile deep, up to 18 miles wide, 277 river miles long, and displays more than 20 layers of rock\\u00a0The layers tell stories of oceans, deserts, mountains, and swamps that were once here, brought into existence, then swept away over the vast expanse of time.\\u00a0<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Grand Canyon is a geologically young landscape being sculpted from very old rocks. Knowing some of the stories encoded in the rock layers enriches your understanding of our planet and enhances your experience at Grand Canyon.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>The program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.\\u00a0\\u00a0The\\u00a0Geology Talk is subject to cancellation due to inclement weather or when lightning danger is present.<\\/p>\\n<\\/div>\\n<div class=\\\"InfoAccordian\\\">\\u00a0<\\/div>\",\"location\":\"Yavapai Point is located on Village Loop Road, in between Market Plaza and the Grand Canyon Visitor Center. From the far end of the Yavapai Point parking lot, by the shuttle bus stop, walk the paved path up the hill on your left to the stone museum building, perched on the edge of the canyon rim. Meet the ranger at 9 am, just outside of the building.\",\"tags\":[\"ranger activity\",\"Ranger Talk\",\"orientation\",\"geology activity\",\"geology\",\"Grand Canyon\",\"Arizona\",\"Village\"],\"types\":[\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20241028T070000Z;UNTIL=20250503T070000Z;FREQ=DAILY;WKST=SU;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-10-20T16:28:45.71\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-01-18T11:53:31.093\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"48e55f61-b589-4ba4-8ea1-3e78530e045d\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"11:00 AM\",\"timeend\":\"11:30 AM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-21\",\"2025-03-22\",\"2025-03-23\",\"2025-03-24\",\"2025-03-25\",\"2025-03-26\",\"2025-03-27\",\"2025-03-28\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-03-30\",\"2025-03-31\",\"2025-04-01\",\"2025-04-02\",\"2025-04-03\",\"2025-04-04\",\"2025-04-05\",\"2025-04-06\",\"2025-04-07\",\"2025-04-08\",\"2025-04-09\",\"2025-04-10\",\"2025-04-11\",\"2025-04-12\",\"2025-04-13\",\"2025-04-14\",\"2025-04-15\",\"2025-04-16\",\"2025-04-17\",\"2025-04-18\",\"2025-04-19\",\"2025-04-20\",\"2025-04-21\",\"2025-04-22\",\"2025-04-23\",\"2025-04-24\",\"2025-04-25\",\"2025-04-26\",\"2025-04-27\",\"2025-04-28\",\"2025-04-29\",\"2025-04-30\",\"2025-05-01\",\"2025-05-02\",\"2025-05-03\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"35339\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/6F754EB9-EFB0-654D-774A8BEEDC74E73F.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/6F754EB9-EFB0-654D-774A8BEEDC74E73F.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"An irregularly-shaped one-story building, approximately 40-feet (12 m) deep by 65-feet (20 m) wide\",\"caption\":\"Meet the ranger here at 2 pm, just outside of the museum building\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\\/M. Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"35346\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/86630DFD-08AC-39F1-63AEA7352DE21262.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/86630DFD-08AC-39F1-63AEA7352DE21262.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"a series of colorful and foreshortened plateaus, cliffs and slopes create two peaks that tower above\",\"caption\":\"Attend the \\\"Geo Glimpse\\\" program to gain insight into Grand Canyon\\u2019s unique geologic story.\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\\/M. Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"35339,35346\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"B42EEF91-F916-DB52-AC44BFB98B748002\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(97,'South Rim Village | History Exhibit: The Amazing Kolb Brothers; A Grand Life at Grand Canyon','nps','952F7EE1-C387-28FE-C26EBD9CC29A5017',5,'For those with an interest in Grand Canyon history, see the Amazing Kolb Brothers Exhibit at Kolb Studio, house-turned-museum perched perilously on a western precipice in Grand Canyon Village. — View the antique cameras used by our pioneer photographers, study paintings by plein-air artists, and watch their 1912 motion picture travelogue, about their exploration of Grand Canyon and river trips down the Colorado River. Nearly demolished in the 1960s, this structure stands today as a park icon, art gallery, and bookstore for visitors in the vicinity of Bright Angel Trail.Currently operated by the park\'s non-profit partner, Grand Canyon Conservancy, visitors can purchase artwork, books, gifts, souvenirs, and basic hiking gear, or simply stop by for park information and the Amazing the Kolb Brothers Exhibit about the life and adventures on the edge of Grand Canyon.\\r\\n\\r\\nKolb Studio is located in the South Rim Village Historic District, on the canyon rim at the head of Bright Angel Trail, and just west of the Bright Angel Lodge cabins. This historic studio is open year-round. It contains an exhibit hall, an information desk, and a Grand Canyon Conservancy Park Store.\n\nThe store features a tribute to the Kolbs\' photographs of mule riders at Grand Canyon. A small exhibit on the top floor tells the Kolb brothers\' story, and displays their early black and white photographs.\n\nThe downstairs gallery features paintings by some of the most renown Grand Canyon Artists during the annual Celebration of Art Exhibit, from mid-September to mid-January.  The Amazing Kolb Brother\'s Exhibit and the 1912 film made by the Kolb brothers, plays in the auditorium the rest of the year.',36.058,-112.143,'grca_information@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/art-exhibits.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-01-23 00:00:00','2025-09-05 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"108214\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2025-01-23\",\"dateend\":\"2025-09-05\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-01-23\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-09-05\",\"latitude\":\"36.057960\",\"longitude\":\"-112.142600\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/art-exhibits.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | History Exhibit: The Amazing Kolb Brothers; A Grand Life at Grand Canyon\",\"contactname\":\"Kolb Studio\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"928-638-2771\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_information@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p>For those with an interest in Grand Canyon history, see the Amazing Kolb Brothers Exhibit at Kolb Studio, house-turned-museum perched perilously on a western precipice in Grand Canyon Village. \\u2014 View\\u00a0the antique cameras used by\\u00a0our pioneer photographers, study paintings by plein-air artists, and watch their 1912\\u00a0motion picture travelogue, about their exploration of Grand Canyon and\\u00a0river trips down the Colorado River.\\u00a0<br \\/><br \\/>Nearly demolished in the 1960s, this structure stands today as a park icon, art gallery, and bookstore for visitors in the vicinity of Bright Angel Trail.<br \\/><br \\/>Currently operated by the park\'s non-profit partner,\\u00a0Grand Canyon Conservancy, visitors can purchase artwork, books, gifts, souvenirs, and basic hiking gear, or simply stop by for park information and the Amazing the Kolb Brothers Exhibit about the life and adventures on the edge of Grand Canyon.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Kolb Studio is located in the South Rim Village Historic District, on the canyon rim at the head of Bright Angel Trail, and just west of the Bright Angel Lodge cabins. This historic studio is open year-round. It contains an exhibit hall, an information desk, and a Grand Canyon Conservancy Park Store.\\n\\nThe store features a tribute to the Kolbs\' photographs of mule riders at Grand Canyon. A small exhibit on the top floor tells the Kolb brothers\' story, and displays their early black and white photographs.\\n\\nThe downstairs gallery features paintings by some of the most renown Grand Canyon Artists during the annual Celebration of Art Exhibit, from mid-September to mid-January.  The Amazing Kolb Brother\'s Exhibit and the 1912 film made by the Kolb brothers, plays in the auditorium the rest of the year.\",\"tags\":[\"Exhibit\",\"hisory\",\"historic building\",\"art collection\",\"photographers\",\"pioneer\",\"book store\",\"shop\",\"overlook\"],\"types\":[\"Exhibition\\/Show\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250123T070000Z;UNTIL=20250905T070000Z;FREQ=DAILY;WKST=SU;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-01-22T11:49:15.603\",\"datetimeupdated\":null,\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"08:00 AM\",\"timeend\":\"06:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-21\",\"2025-03-22\",\"2025-03-23\",\"2025-03-24\",\"2025-03-25\",\"2025-03-26\",\"2025-03-27\",\"2025-03-28\",\"2025-03-29\",\"2025-03-30\",\"2025-03-31\",\"2025-04-01\",\"2025-04-02\",\"2025-04-03\",\"2025-04-04\",\"2025-04-05\",\"2025-04-06\",\"2025-04-07\",\"2025-04-08\",\"2025-04-09\",\"2025-04-10\",\"2025-04-11\",\"2025-04-12\",\"2025-04-13\",\"2025-04-14\",\"2025-04-15\",\"2025-04-16\",\"2025-04-17\",\"2025-04-18\",\"2025-04-19\",\"2025-04-20\",\"2025-04-21\",\"2025-04-22\",\"2025-04-23\",\"2025-04-24\",\"2025-04-25\",\"2025-04-26\",\"2025-04-27\",\"2025-04-28\",\"2025-04-29\",\"2025-04-30\",\"2025-05-01\",\"2025-05-02\",\"2025-05-03\",\"2025-05-04\",\"2025-05-05\",\"2025-05-06\",\"2025-05-07\",\"2025-05-08\",\"2025-05-09\",\"2025-05-10\",\"2025-05-11\",\"2025-05-12\",\"2025-05-13\",\"2025-05-14\",\"2025-05-15\",\"2025-05-16\",\"2025-05-17\",\"2025-05-18\",\"2025-05-19\",\"2025-05-20\",\"2025-05-21\",\"2025-05-22\",\"2025-05-23\",\"2025-05-24\",\"2025-05-25\",\"2025-05-26\",\"2025-05-27\",\"2025-05-28\",\"2025-05-29\",\"2025-05-30\",\"2025-05-31\",\"2025-06-01\",\"2025-06-02\",\"2025-06-03\",\"2025-06-04\",\"2025-06-05\",\"2025-06-06\",\"2025-06-07\",\"2025-06-08\",\"2025-06-09\",\"2025-06-10\",\"2025-06-11\",\"2025-06-12\",\"2025-06-13\",\"2025-06-14\",\"2025-06-15\",\"2025-06-16\",\"2025-06-17\",\"2025-06-18\",\"2025-06-19\",\"2025-06-20\",\"2025-06-21\",\"2025-06-22\",\"2025-06-23\",\"2025-06-24\",\"2025-06-25\",\"2025-06-26\",\"2025-06-27\",\"2025-06-28\",\"2025-06-29\",\"2025-06-30\",\"2025-07-01\",\"2025-07-02\",\"2025-07-03\",\"2025-07-04\",\"2025-07-05\",\"2025-07-06\",\"2025-07-07\",\"2025-07-08\",\"2025-07-09\",\"2025-07-10\",\"2025-07-11\",\"2025-07-12\",\"2025-07-13\",\"2025-07-14\",\"2025-07-15\",\"2025-07-16\",\"2025-07-17\",\"2025-07-18\",\"2025-07-19\",\"2025-07-20\",\"2025-07-21\",\"2025-07-22\",\"2025-07-23\",\"2025-07-24\",\"2025-07-25\",\"2025-07-26\",\"2025-07-27\",\"2025-07-28\",\"2025-07-29\",\"2025-07-30\",\"2025-07-31\",\"2025-08-01\",\"2025-08-02\",\"2025-08-03\",\"2025-08-04\",\"2025-08-05\",\"2025-08-06\",\"2025-08-07\",\"2025-08-08\",\"2025-08-09\",\"2025-08-10\",\"2025-08-11\",\"2025-08-12\",\"2025-08-13\",\"2025-08-14\",\"2025-08-15\",\"2025-08-16\",\"2025-08-17\",\"2025-08-18\",\"2025-08-19\",\"2025-08-20\",\"2025-08-21\",\"2025-08-22\",\"2025-08-23\",\"2025-08-24\",\"2025-08-25\",\"2025-08-26\",\"2025-08-27\",\"2025-08-28\",\"2025-08-29\",\"2025-08-30\",\"2025-08-31\",\"2025-09-01\",\"2025-09-02\",\"2025-09-03\",\"2025-09-04\",\"2025-09-05\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"31081\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/74A1E415-B3E9-DA45-C47ADFD4B9A695A9.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/74A1E415-B3E9-DA45-C47ADFD4B9A695A9.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Looking across an exhibit hall with paintings and exhibit panels on the walls\",\"caption\":\"The Amazing Kolb Brothers Exhibit: A Grand Life at Grand Canyon\",\"credit\":\"NPS\\/M.Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"31082\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/74E5037F-FACC-6484-993799FC10CF65D4.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/74E5037F-FACC-6484-993799FC10CF65D4.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Wood frame building nestled by oak trees is overlooking sunset falling on colorful peaks and cliffs.\",\"caption\":\"Historic Kolb Studio on the South Rim of Grand Canyon National Park\",\"credit\":\"NPS\\/M.Quinn\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"31081,31082\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"952F7EE1-C387-28FE-C26EBD9CC29A5017\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(98,'South Rim Village | Evening Program - Interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie, the park\'s Tribal Program Coordinator','nps','E148CEC2-F625-56D8-ECFF4521B6E3C257',5,'Visitor Center Theater Evening Program 7 to 8 pmEvening Program - An Interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie\nGrand Canyon Speaks Podcast presents an insightful interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie, a fourth-generation National Park Service employee. With her roots on the Navajo Nation in Arizona, she now serves as the Tribal Program Coordinator for Grand Canyon National Park.  \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.',36.0591,-112.109,'grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/learn/historyculture/associated-tribes.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-24 00:00:00','2025-03-24 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"110380\",\"date\":\"2025-03-24\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-24\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-24\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-24\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-24\",\"latitude\":\"36.059095\",\"longitude\":\"-112.108899\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/learn\\/historyculture\\/associated-tribes.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Evening Program - Interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie, the park\'s Tribal Program Coordinator\",\"contactname\":\"Cultural Demonstration Program\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p>Visitor Center Theater Evening Program 7 to 8 pm<br \\/><strong>Evening Program - An Interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<div data-ogsc=\\\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\\\">Grand Canyon Speaks Podcast presents an insightful interview with Kelkiyana Yazzie, a fourth-generation National Park Service employee. With her roots on the Navajo Nation in Arizona, she now serves as the Tribal Program Coordinator for Grand Canyon National Park.\\u00a0\\u00a0<\\/div>\",\"location\":\"From the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.\",\"tags\":[\"evening program\",\"NPS Indigenous\",\"Grand Canyon First Voices\",\"Grand Canyon\",\"Navajo Nation\"],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Living History\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-19T16:37:27.173\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-19T16:38:04.403\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"800e488e-04fd-43a8-b19d-7b242d2f21b2\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"07:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"08:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-24\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"36755\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Map shows location of 4 public parking lots in relation to and surrounding the Visitor Center Plaza.\",\"caption\":\"Meet at the Visitor Center Theater, in the Visitor Center Building, in the center of the map.\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"36756\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"a large, curved visitor center building with blue doors and solar panels on a gray sloping roof.\",\"caption\":\"Grand Canyon Visitor Center, location of the theater where the evening program will be presented.\",\"credit\":\"NPS photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"},{\"imageid\":\"46459\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/E11F602F-E808-E1AD-D83C6A04A6811E43.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/E11F602F-E808-E1AD-D83C6A04A6811E43.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"A young Indigenous woman wearing a park ranger uniform with a turquoise squash blossom necklace.\",\"caption\":\"Kelkiyana Yazzie\",\"credit\":\"NPS\\/B. Maul\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"3\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"36755,36756,46459\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"E148CEC2-F625-56D8-ECFF4521B6E3C257\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(99,'South Rim: Desert View | Cultural Demonstrations with Lynn & Jane Quam (Zuni stone carvers)','nps','E5786305-00DA-6290-C4087404DAF43E8E',5,'Tuesday and Wednesday — March 25 and 26, 2025 \nLynn & Jane Quam (Zuni stone carvers)\nMeet Jayne and Lynn Quam, Zuni Stone Carvers, at the Watchtower from 9 am to 4 pm.\n\nThey have been creating traditional Zuni fetishes for over 30 years and have won multiple awards for their work.\n\n\n\"In 1980 I carved my first animal fetish and received an order for more,\" Jayne says. \"A few years later we began going to shows. As the years go by, we gain new experiences with different stones. Our ideas for new designs are coming to life every day.”\n\n\n\n\n\"I carve all kinds of animals. My favorite pieces to carve are buffalos and bears,\" Lynn says. \n\n\n\nMeet and talk with the demonstrators while they create and showcase their art at the Desert View Watchtower on the South Rim at the Desert View developed area at the eastern entrance to the park. \n\nThe Cultural Demonstration program provides an opportunity for park visitors and community members to interact with tribal artisans from Grand Canyon\'s traditionally associated tribes - and for them to share their history and crafts, along with the skills, knowledge, and efforts involved in creating their craft and art.  \nThis series is made possible with grants from Grand Canyon Conservancy.\\r\\n\\r\\nMeet our demonstrators inside on the first floor of the Desert View Watchtower.',36.0441,-111.826,'grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/desert-view-cultural-demonstration-program.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-25 00:00:00','2025-03-26 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"110210\",\"date\":\"2025-03-25\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-25\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-26\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-25\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-26\",\"latitude\":\"36.044100\",\"longitude\":\"-111.826161\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/desert-view-cultural-demonstration-program.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"Demonstrators will be inside the Desert View Watchtower from 9 am - 4 pm.\",\"title\":\"South Rim: Desert View | Cultural Demonstrations with Lynn & Jane Quam (Zuni stone carvers)\",\"contactname\":\"Cultural Demonstration Program\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p>Tuesday and Wednesday\\u00a0\\u2014\\u00a0March 25 and 26, 2025\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Lynn &amp; Jane Quam (Zuni\\u00a0stone carvers)<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p>Meet Jayne and Lynn Quam, Zuni Stone Carvers, at the Watchtower from 9 am to 4 pm.<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>They have been creating traditional Zuni fetishes for over 30 years and have won multiple awards for their work.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\\"In 1980 I carved my first animal fetish and received an order for more,\\\" Jayne says. \\\"A few years later we began going to shows. As the years go by, we gain new experiences with different stones. Our ideas for new designs are coming to life every day.\\u201d<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<ul>\\n<li>\\n<div class=\\\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\\\">\\n<div dir=\\\"auto\\\">\\\"I carve all kinds of animals. My favorite pieces to carve are buffalos and bears,\\\" Lynn says.\\u00a0<\\/div>\\n<\\/div>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Meet and\\u00a0talk with\\u00a0the demonstrators while they create and showcase their art at the Desert View Watchtower on the South Rim at the Desert View developed area\\u00a0at the eastern entrance to the park.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-leveltext=\\\"\\uf0b7\\\" data-font=\\\"Symbol\\\" data-listid=\\\"27\\\" data-aria-posinset=\\\"2\\\" data-aria-level=\\\"1\\\"><span data-contrast=\\\"auto\\\">The Cultural Demonstration program provides an opportunity for park visitors and community members to interact with tribal artisans from Grand Canyon\'s traditionally associated tribes - and for them to share their history and crafts, along with the skills, knowledge, and efforts involved in creating\\u00a0their craft and art.\\u00a0<br \\/><\\/span><span data-ccp-props=\\\"{&quot;134233279&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:160,&quot;335559740&quot;:257}\\\">\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/li>\\n<li data-leveltext=\\\"\\uf0b7\\\" data-font=\\\"Symbol\\\" data-listid=\\\"27\\\" data-aria-posinset=\\\"3\\\" data-aria-level=\\\"1\\\"><span data-contrast=\\\"auto\\\">This series is made possible with grants from Grand Canyon Conservancy.<\\/span><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\",\"location\":\"Meet our demonstrators inside on the first floor of the Desert View Watchtower.\",\"tags\":[\"cultural demo\",\"desert view\",\"Zuni\",\"Meet the artist\",\"Carving Decorative arts\",\"native artist\",\"handmade\"],\"types\":[\"Cultural\\/Craft Demonstration\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250325T070000Z;UNTIL=20250326T070000Z;FREQ=DAILY;WKST=SU;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-14T19:16:30.507\",\"datetimeupdated\":null,\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"\",\"risdpoiid\":\"949c3ebf-a5db-44b4-ba5b-5c681cffa814\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"09:00 AM\",\"timeend\":\"04:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-25\",\"2025-03-26\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"43251\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/AB941724-D8DE-4FB3-BDC7634562C23B59.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/AB941724-D8DE-4FB3-BDC7634562C23B59.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"A circular stone tower, four stories high, on the edge of a vast canyon cliff. Around the circumfere\",\"caption\":\"Cultura Demonstrations take place at Desert View Watchtower\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"46412\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/E5594F2A-F46A-7F02-B9BCD60E7A709E33.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/E5594F2A-F46A-7F02-B9BCD60E7A709E33.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Three precious stone bear carvings, one round, one arched, and the third with an elongated neck.\",\"caption\":\"Zuni bear fetish carvings by Lynn & Jayne Quam\",\"credit\":\"NPS photos\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"43251,46412\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"E5786305-00DA-6290-C4087404DAF43E8E\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(100,'South Rim Village | Havasupai dance group performance - along the Canyon Rim Trail by Hopi House','nps','213D2C23-FB0E-837C-59C7703649D464DA',5,'Guardians of the Grand Canyon A Havasupai dance group performance\n - Along the Canyon Rim Trail by Hopi House - Outdoors \nThursday March 27, 2025 - Please join us for a special performance by the Guardians of the Grand Canyon, a traditional and multigenerational group, showcasing the rich traditions of Indigenous dance.\nThe Havasuw Baaja, meaning \"the people of the blue-green waters,\" are the traditional guardians of the Grand Canyon. The Havasupai people have lived in the stunning riparian landscape, 3,000 feet below the South Rim since time immemorial. Don’t miss this chance to learn, share, and celebrate! \nTime: 10 a.m. to 11 a.m. The program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.\\r\\n\\r\\nLocated in the Village HIstoric District, opposite El Tovar hotel, on the other side of the large circular driveway, Hopi House is a three-story stepped stone masonry structure with sandstone walls with parapets. Hopi House is adjacent to the Canyon Rim Trail, that runs alongside the north end of the building, overlooking the canyon landscape.',36.0582,-112.137,'grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/calendar.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-27 00:00:00','2025-03-27 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Special Event\",\"eventid\":\"110447\",\"date\":\"2025-03-27\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-27\",\"latitude\":\"36.058198\",\"longitude\":\"-112.136657\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/calendar.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Havasupai dance group performance - along the Canyon Rim Trail by Hopi House\",\"contactname\":\"Kelli Jones\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"928-638-7893\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Guardians of the Grand Canyon A Havasupai dance group performance<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p><strong> - Along the Canyon Rim Trail by Hopi House - Outdoors<\\/strong>\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Thursday March 27, 2025 -<span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW261624593 BCX8\\\">\\u00a0Please join us for a special performance by the Guardians of the Grand Canyon, a traditional and multigenerational group,\\u00a0<\\/span><span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW261624593 BCX8\\\">showcasing<\\/span><span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW261624593 BCX8\\\"> the rich traditions of Indigenous dance.<\\/span><\\/p>\\n<p>The Havasuw Baaja, meaning \\\"the people of the blue-green waters,\\\" are the traditional guardians of the Grand Canyon. The Havasupai people have lived in the stunning riparian landscape, 3,000 feet below the South Rim since time immemorial. Don\\u2019t miss this chance to learn, share, and celebrate!\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Time:\\u00a010\\u00a0a.m. to\\u00a011\\u00a0a.m.\\u00a0<\\/strong><br \\/><br \\/>The program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"Located in the Village HIstoric District, opposite El Tovar hotel, on the other side of the large circular driveway, Hopi House is a three-story stepped stone masonry structure with sandstone walls with parapets. Hopi House is adjacent to the Canyon Rim Trail, that runs alongside the north end of the building, overlooking the canyon landscape.\",\"tags\":[\"Outdoor activities\",\"Village\",\"Havasupai\",\"Cultural Dancer\",\"Live Performance\",\"indigenous heritage\",\"dance\"],\"types\":[\"Talk\",\"Walk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-20T22:25:40.697\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-20T22:28:29.063\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":null,\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"10:00 AM\",\"timeend\":\"11:00 AM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-27\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"46470\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/212DDC43-B1EB-5FA5-2FE20CAB783FBE44.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/212DDC43-B1EB-5FA5-2FE20CAB783FBE44.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"9 Havasupai adults and a boy, dressed in colorful ceremonial clothes are posing for a group photo.\",\"caption\":\"Guardians of Grand Canyon, Havasupai Dance Group.\",\"credit\":\"NPS\\/photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"44951\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/1F9A2F9A-C495-986D-1F12E7ED383B7478.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/1F9A2F9A-C495-986D-1F12E7ED383B7478.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"a three-story stepped stone masonry structure with sandstone walls with parapets.\",\"caption\":\"Hopi House is adjacent to the Canyon Rim Trail, that runs alongside the north end of the building, overlooking the canyon landscape.\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"46470,44951\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"213D2C23-FB0E-837C-59C7703649D464DA\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(101,'South Rim Village | Havasupai Dance Group Performance - Visitor Center Plaza','nps','205DC616-AA1B-4C86-C6BB92F2E4AE6EF9',5,'Guardians of the Grand Canyon A Havasupai dance group performance - Visitor Center Plaza - Outdoors\n\nThursday March 27, 2025 - Outdoors on the Visitor Center Plaza, Please join us for a special performance by the Guardians of the Grand Canyon, a traditional and multigenerational group.\nThe Havasuw Baaja, meaning \"the people of the blue-green waters,\" are the traditional guardians of the Grand Canyon. The Havasupai people have lived in the stunning riparian landscape, 3,000 feet below the South Rim since time immemorial. Don’t miss this chance to learn, share, and celebrate! \n\nTime: 2 p.m. to 3 p.m. \nLocation: South Rim - Grand Canyon Visitor Center Plaza, next to the Visitor Center Theater.\nThe program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.',36.0591,-112.109,'grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/calendar.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-27 00:00:00','2025-03-27 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Special Event\",\"eventid\":\"110446\",\"date\":\"2025-03-27\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-27\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-27\",\"latitude\":\"36.059095\",\"longitude\":\"-112.108899\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/planyourvisit\\/calendar.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Havasupai Dance Group Performance - Visitor Center Plaza\",\"contactname\":\"Kelli Jones\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"928-638-7893\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p><strong> Guardians of the Grand Canyon A Havasupai dance group performance <br \\/>-\\u00a0Visitor Center Plaza - Outdoors<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li data-leveltext=\\\"\\uf0b7\\\" data-font=\\\"Symbol\\\" data-listid=\\\"161\\\" data-list-defn-props=\\\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559683&quot;:0,&quot;335559684&quot;:-2,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;\\uf0b7&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\\\" data-aria-posinset=\\\"2\\\" data-aria-level=\\\"1\\\"><span data-contrast=\\\"auto\\\"><strong>Thursday March 27, 2025<\\/strong> - Outdoors on the Visitor Center Plaza, Please join us for a special performance by the <strong>Guardians of the Grand Canyon<\\/strong>, a traditional and multigenerational group.<\\/span><span data-ccp-props=\\\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\\\"><br \\/><br \\/><\\/span><\\/li>\\n<li data-leveltext=\\\"\\uf0b7\\\" data-font=\\\"Symbol\\\" data-listid=\\\"161\\\" data-list-defn-props=\\\"{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559683&quot;:0,&quot;335559684&quot;:-2,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;\\uf0b7&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}\\\" data-aria-posinset=\\\"2\\\" data-aria-level=\\\"1\\\"><span class=\\\"TextRun SCXW121574985 BCX8\\\" lang=\\\"EN-US\\\" xml:lang=\\\"EN-US\\\" data-contrast=\\\"auto\\\"><span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW121574985 BCX8\\\">The Havasuw Baaja, meaning \\\"the people of the blue-green waters,\\\" are the traditional guardians of the Grand Canyon. The Havasupai people have lived in the stunning riparian landscape, 3,000 feet below the South Rim since time immemorial. <\\/span><span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW121574985 BCX8\\\">Don\\u2019t<\\/span><span class=\\\"NormalTextRun SCXW121574985 BCX8\\\"> miss this chance to learn, share, and celebrate!<\\/span><\\/span><span class=\\\"EOP SCXW121574985 BCX8\\\" data-ccp-props=\\\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\\\">\\u00a0<\\/span><\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p><strong>Time:\\u00a02 p.m. to\\u00a03 p.m.\\u00a0<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<p><strong>Location:<\\/strong>\\u00a0South Rim - Grand Canyon Visitor Center Plaza, next to the Visitor Center Theater.<\\/p>\\n<p>The program is free of charge. Children must be accompanied by an adult.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"From the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.\",\"tags\":[\"NPS Indigenous\",\"indigenous knowledge\",\"Grand Canyon First Voices\",\"indigenous heritage\",\"Havasupai\",\"Native American dances\",\"dance\",\"Live Performance\"],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Living History\",\"Performance\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-20T22:01:16.693\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-20T22:27:10.627\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"800e488e-04fd-43a8-b19d-7b242d2f21b2\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"02:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"03:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-27\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"46469\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/2085DCCC-F327-D8DD-218AA28FEECF99EA.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/2085DCCC-F327-D8DD-218AA28FEECF99EA.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"9 Havasupai adults and a boy, dressed in colorful ceremonial clothes and posing for a group photo.\",\"caption\":\"Guardians of Grand Canyon, Havasupai Dance Group.\",\"credit\":\"NPS photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"36755\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Map shows location of 4 public parking lots in relation to and surrounding the Visitor Center Plaza.\",\"caption\":\"Meet at the Visitor Center Theater, in the Visitor Center Building, in the center of the map.\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"},{\"imageid\":\"36756\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"a large, curved visitor center building with blue doors and solar panels on a gray sloping roof.\",\"caption\":\"Grand Canyon Visitor Center, location of the theater where the evening program will be presented.\",\"credit\":\"NPS photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"3\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"46469,36755,36756\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"205DC616-AA1B-4C86-C6BB92F2E4AE6EF9\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(102,'South Rim Village | Evening Program - Interview with Kelli Jones, Interpretive Ranger at Desert View','nps','EF330EEA-C3A6-F066-9346844336156C68',5,'Visitor Center Theater Evening Program 7 to 8 pmEvening Program - An Interview with Kelli Jones, Park Ranger\nGrand Canyon Speaks Podcast presents an interview with Kelli Jones, Interpretive Park Ranger at Desert View. Kelli focuses on the Indigenous History and stories of the tribal communitiies that have lived in and around Grand Canyon since time immemorial. Kelli says, “We wouldn’t be here today if it weren’t for the stories, songs and prayers of Grand Canyon.\"\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.',36.0591,-112.109,'grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov',NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/grca/learn/historyculture/associated-tribes.htm',NULL,NULL,'2025-03-31 00:00:00','2025-03-31 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"110394\",\"date\":\"2025-03-31\",\"datestart\":\"2025-03-31\",\"dateend\":\"2025-03-31\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-03-31\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-03-31\",\"latitude\":\"36.059095\",\"longitude\":\"-112.108899\",\"isrecurring\":\"false\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/grca\\/learn\\/historyculture\\/associated-tribes.htm\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"\",\"title\":\"South Rim Village | Evening Program - Interview with Kelli Jones, Interpretive Ranger at Desert View\",\"contactname\":\"Cultural Demonstration Program\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"grca_cultural_expressions_program@nps.gov\",\"description\":\"<p>Visitor Center Theater Evening Program 7 to 8 pm<br \\/><strong>Evening Program - An Interview with Kelli Jones,\\u00a0Park Ranger<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<div data-ogsc=\\\"rgb(0, 0, 0)\\\">Grand Canyon Speaks Podcast presents an interview with Kelli Jones, Interpretive Park Ranger at Desert View. Kelli focuses\\u00a0on the Indigenous History and stories of the tribal communitiies\\u00a0that have lived\\u00a0in and around Grand Canyon since time immemorial. Kelli says, \\u201cWe wouldn\\u2019t be here today if it weren\\u2019t for the stories, songs and prayers of Grand Canyon.\\\"<\\/div>\",\"location\":\"From the South Entrance Station, continue following the road you are on for 5 miles, and it will lead you to the Visitor Center. Just before the parking areas, the road curves to the left. You can park your vehicle in one of four parking areas and find your way to the Visitor Center, in the center of the open plaza where restroom buildings, the park store, and the bicycle rental are also located. View the map below.\",\"tags\":[\"evening program\",\"NPS Indigenous\",\"Grand Canyon First Voices\",\"Grand Canyon\",\"Navajo Nation\"],\"types\":[\"Campfire\\/Evening Program\",\"Living History\",\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"\",\"sitecode\":\"grca\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2025-03-19T23:06:31.793\",\"datetimeupdated\":\"2025-03-19T23:13:24.99\",\"createuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"updateuser\":\"mquinn@nps.gov\",\"risdpoiid\":\"800e488e-04fd-43a8-b19d-7b242d2f21b2\",\"times\":[{\"timestart\":\"07:00 PM\",\"timeend\":\"08:00 PM\",\"sunrisestart\":\"false\",\"sunsetend\":\"false\"}],\"dates\":[\"2025-03-31\"],\"images\":[{\"imageid\":\"36755\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/213A61C8-CE77-8950-E621313FB52B877F.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"Map shows location of 4 public parking lots in relation to and surrounding the Visitor Center Plaza.\",\"caption\":\"Meet at the Visitor Center Theater, in the Visitor Center Building, in the center of the map.\",\"credit\":\"NPS\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"1\"},{\"imageid\":\"36756\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/215B2112-9C5D-FFD1-AD33D490CF3A25B0.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"a large, curved visitor center building with blue doors and solar panels on a gray sloping roof.\",\"caption\":\"Grand Canyon Visitor Center, location of the theater where the evening program will be presented.\",\"credit\":\"NPS photo\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"2\"},{\"imageid\":\"46462\",\"path\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/EF066F3A-CC7A-D5A0-2358DEFFA8FBFDA6.jpg\",\"url\":\"\\/common\\/uploads\\/event_calendar\\/EF066F3A-CC7A-D5A0-2358DEFFA8FBFDA6.jpg\",\"title\":\"\",\"altText\":\"A Din\\u00e9 woman wearing a National Park Service uniform is posing for a photo in front of a vast canyon\",\"caption\":\"Kelli Jones, Interpretive park ranger at Desert View.\",\"credit\":\"Photo: Kelli Jones\",\"id\":\"\",\"ordinal\":\"3\"}],\"imageidlist\":\"36755,36756,46462\",\"subjectname\":\"\",\"parkfullname\":\"Grand Canyon National Park\",\"portalname\":\"\",\"organizationname\":\"\",\"id\":\"EF330EEA-C3A6-F066-9346844336156C68\"}',1,'2025-03-21 18:08:54','2025-03-21 18:08:54'),(103,'Visitor Center Ranger Talk','nps','92EAAEFE-EC19-E477-994A68A93A5F65E8',6,'Discover the survival secrets of desert plants and animals, learn how the geologic scenery came to be, hear the human history of the park, and more. \nExplore the fascinating world of Zion’s wildlife and learn their survival secrets or discover the stories of the people who lived in and helped shape Zion. Subjects vary, so no two programs are quite the same. This program is accessible.\n \nAccessibility information\nThis program takes place outdoors on a partially-shaded patio. Stone benches are available for seating, as well as space for mobility devices. Rangers at the visitor center are available for any additional questions. You can also visit the Accessibility page of our website for more information.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis ranger talk takes place at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center amphitheater.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-02-09 00:00:00','2025-05-17 00:00:00','{\"categoryid\":\"1\",\"category\":\"Regular Event\",\"eventid\":\"106571\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21\",\"datestart\":\"2025-02-09\",\"dateend\":\"2025-05-17\",\"recurrencedatestart\":\"2025-02-09\",\"recurrencedateend\":\"2025-05-17\",\"latitude\":\"\",\"longitude\":\"\",\"isrecurring\":\"true\",\"isallday\":\"false\",\"isregresrequired\":\"false\",\"isfree\":\"true\",\"regresurl\":\"\",\"regresinfo\":\"\",\"infourl\":\"\",\"feeinfo\":\"\",\"timeinfo\":\"Park entrance fees apply.\",\"title\":\"Visitor Center Ranger Talk\",\"contactname\":\"\",\"contacttelephonenumber\":\"\",\"contactemailaddress\":\"\",\"description\":\"<p>Discover the survival secrets of desert plants and animals, learn how the geologic scenery came to be, hear the human history of the park, and more.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Explore the fascinating world of Zion\\u2019s wildlife and learn their survival secrets or discover the stories of the people who lived in and helped shape Zion. Subjects vary, so no two programs are quite the same.\\u00a0This program is accessible.<\\/p>\\n<p>\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Accessibility information<\\/p>\\n<p>This program takes place outdoors on a partially-shaded patio. Stone benches are available for seating, as well as space for mobility devices. Rangers at the visitor center are available for any additional questions. You can also visit the\\u00a0<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/zion\\/planyourvisit\\/accessibility.htm\\\">Accessibility page\\u00a0<\\/a>of our website for more information.<\\/p>\",\"location\":\"This ranger talk takes place at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center amphitheater.\",\"tags\":[\"Rangers\",\"Ranger program\",\"programs\",\"interp\",\"education\",\"interpretation\",\"ranger talk\",\"presentation\"],\"types\":[\"Talk\"],\"recurrencerule\":\"DTSTART=20250209T070000Z;UNTIL=20250517T060000Z;FREQ=DAILY;WKST=SU;COUNT=0;INTERVAL=1\",\"sitecode\":\"zion\",\"sitetype\":\"park\",\"datetimecreated\":\"2024-12-03T17:43:08.16\"